                <pb facs="0755" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/2056: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in Sweden
                        (Johnson)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-11T23:00:00-04:00">March 11, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>135. Your 447, March 6, 8 p.m., and your 456, March 7, 2 p.m. The Department is
                    gratified at the progress being made in the plan for the relief of Greece and
                    hopes that arrangements along the lines of Mr. Boheman’s suggestions may be put
                    into effect at the earliest possible date.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
